Templates - C++ - metaprogramming
It is possible to do metaprogramming with templates and therefore use templates to compute something during compile time. It heavily depends on recursion

Code file template_meta.cpp
#include &lt;iostream&gt;

// Template metaprogramming for calculationg factorial at compile-time
template &lt;int N&gt; struct Factorial {
  static const int value = N * Factorial&lt;N - 1&gt;::value;
};

// Specialization for the base class (Factorial&lt;0&gt;)
template &lt;&gt; struct Factorial&lt;0&gt; {
  static const int value = 1;
};

int main() {

  // Factorial computation happens at compile-time
  std::cout &lt;&lt; "Factorial of 5 is: " &lt;&lt; Factorial&lt;5&gt;::value &lt;&lt; std::endl;

  return 0;
}


Factorial of 5 is: 120

How to include








Form
Search Order
Use Case




#include &lt;header&gt;
System include paths only
Standard library headers or third-party libraries installed in system paths.


#include "header"
Current directory first, then system include paths
Project-specific headers or headers in the same directory.


#include &lt;folder/header&gt;
System include paths only
Third-party libraries with organized subdirectories.


#include "folder/header"
Current directory first, then system include paths
Project-specific headers in subdirectories.


#include &lt;absolute/path&gt;
No search; directly includes the file from the specified absolute path
Rarely used; for debugging or non-standard locations.


#include "relative/path"
Current directory or relative to the file, then system include paths
Headers in parent or sibling directories.

